From: ramin <lordrasmus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv32: allow NPTL without an MMU

Experimental: riscv keeps the thread pointer in tp, which userspace sets
itself and clone (CLONE_SETTLS) sets for new threads, so the kernel side
needs nothing noMMU-specific.  Lets openadk build a rv32 noMMU toolchain
with real TLS.

---
 extra/Configs/Config.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extra/Configs/Config.in b/extra/Configs/Config.in
--- a/extra/Configs/Config.in
+++ b/extra/Configs/Config.in
@@ -623,7 +623,7 @@ config UCLIBC_HAS_THREADS_NATIVE
 		   !TARGET_h8300 && \
 		   !TARGET_hppa && \
 		   !TARGET_ia64 && \
-		   (ARCH_USE_MMU || TARGET_arm || TARGET_xtensa)
+		   (ARCH_USE_MMU || TARGET_arm || TARGET_xtensa || TARGET_riscv32)
 	help
 	  If you want to compile uClibc with NPTL support, then answer Y.
 
